    dc:identifier ns27:WP4560 ;
    dc:source "WikiPathways" ;
    dc:title "MFAP5 effect on permeability and motility of endothelial cells via cytoskeleton rearrangement"@en ;
    dcterms:description """Proposed signaling pathways by which MFAP5 induces LPP expression and increases the permeability and motility of endothelial cells via cytoskeleton rearrangement.
The activation of the MFAP5-mediated signaling cascade in endothelial cells up-regulates LPP expression and subsequently promotes the motility of endothelial cells and the permeability of the endothelial cell monolayer. 

Adapted from supplemental figure 11 from [Leung et al](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5785271/).""" ;
